From f0ac89f4efe099ca0f76c04cef14f41c91261c05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velox <velox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:09:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: complete vkResetDescriptorPool in the guest
 (batched descriptor updates)

With VulkanBatchedDescriptorSetUpdate the guest already owns the pool
accounting: sets are allocated and written locally and only reach the
host when a queue submit commits them. vkResetDescriptorPool was still
a synchronous host round trip (about 33 us on WHPX + goldfish pipe) and
the top cost of Unreal's RHIThread in AnTuTu.

Add vkQueueCommitDescriptorSetUpdates2GOOGLE, which carries one reset
epoch per pool. vkResetDescriptorPool now clears the guest bookkeeping,
increments the pool's epoch and returns VK_SUCCESS (the only result the
specification defines besides the generic VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN; the
application must not reset a pool whose sets are still in use). The
host resets its pool before servicing a commit whose epoch is newer
than the last applied one. Every commit of a pool carries its epoch and
the host executes the commands of a process in encoding order, so the
reset is applied exactly once and before any host allocation made after
it, whichever thread submits.

Used only when the host advertises
ANDROID_EMU_vulkan_deferred_descriptor_pool_reset and queue submit with
commands is on; debug.velox.defer_pool_reset=0 turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I21f017da4bd6725145d72d40ae1c3cf4359873f1
